        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 900,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 808,
        "paragraph_id": "70814351",
        "text": "Where  is the angle between the fluid velocity vector and the x-axis. Finally, it is possible to adjust the initiation of motion criteria for the total transport (keyword bdslpeffini = total) or the bed load transport only (keyword bdslpeffini = bed) through (Soulsby, 1997):"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 32903,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 904,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 812,
        "paragraph_id": "448EDDF4",
        "text": "In this equation is ψ the difference in angle between the flow direction and the on-slope directed vector, β the bed slope and ϕi the angle of repose."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 32945,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 906,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 814,
        "paragraph_id": "022BE6F9",
        "text": "De Vet (2014) provides a detailed overview on how the bed slope and flow direction are calculated and how the bed slope effect is combined with the dilatancy concept if the adjustment to the initiation of motion is considered (Section 2.7.5)."
      }
    ],
    "table_cell": null,
